export const heroSvg = "<svg class=\"art\" viewBox=\"0 0 1280 460\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"The same damaged upright seen two ways: on the manual side it may go unlogged with only paper and memory; on the digital side it is photo-tagged, located and escalated\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\">\n    <rect width=\"1280\" height=\"460\" fill=\"#0B1016\"/>\n    <line x1=\"640\" y1=\"70\" x2=\"640\" y2=\"400\" stroke=\"#141B24\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 6\"/>\n    <text x=\"320\" y=\"52\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"IBM Plex Mono,monospace\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"600\" letter-spacing=\"2\" fill=\"#8B95A1\">MANUAL</text>\n    <text x=\"960\" y=\"52\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"IBM Plex Mono,monospace\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"600\" letter-spacing=\"2\" fill=\"#D95A00\">DIGITAL</text>\n    <!-- floor -->\n    <line x1=\"120\" y1=\"360\" x2=\"560\" y2=\"360\" stroke=\"#2F3A47\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n    <line x1=\"740\" y1=\"360\" x2=\"1180\" y2=\"360\" stroke=\"#2F3A47\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n    <!-- LEFT manual rack (muted) -->\n    <g stroke=\"#4D5A69\" stroke-width=\"6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" fill=\"none\">\n      <line x1=\"230\" y1=\"120\" x2=\"230\" y2=\"360\"/>\n      <polyline points=\"450,120 450,250 466,305 452,360\"/>\n    </g>\n    <g fill=\"#2F3A47\"><rect x=\"224\" y=\"160\" width=\"232\" height=\"7\" rx=\"2\"/><rect x=\"224\" y=\"255\" width=\"232\" height=\"7\" rx=\"2\"/></g>\n    <rect x=\"250\" y=\"120\" width=\"180\" height=\"38\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#141B24\"/>\n    <!-- unnoticed damage: grey ? -->\n    <circle cx=\"500\" cy=\"300\" r=\"17\" fill=\"#141B24\" stroke=\"#4D5A69\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"500\" y=\"306\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"IBM Plex Sans,sans-serif\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#8B95A1\">?</text>\n    <!-- paper note icon -->\n    <g><rect x=\"150\" y=\"250\" width=\"60\" height=\"78\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#0B1016\" stroke=\"#2F3A47\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"162\" y1=\"270\" x2=\"198\" y2=\"270\" stroke=\"#2F3A47\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><line x1=\"162\" y1=\"284\" x2=\"198\" y2=\"284\" stroke=\"#2F3A47\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><line x1=\"162\" y1=\"298\" x2=\"188\" y2=\"298\" stroke=\"#2F3A47\" stroke-width=\"3\"/></g>\n    <text x=\"340\" y=\"398\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"IBM Plex Sans,sans-serif\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#8B95A1\">Damage may go unlogged</text>\n    <!-- RIGHT digital rack (brand) -->\n    <g stroke=\"#C9D1DA\" stroke-width=\"6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" fill=\"none\">\n      <line x1=\"850\" y1=\"120\" x2=\"850\" y2=\"360\"/>\n      <polyline points=\"1070,120 1070,250 1086,305 1072,360\"/>\n    </g>\n    <g fill=\"#C9D1DA\"><rect x=\"844\" y=\"160\" width=\"232\" height=\"7\" rx=\"2\"/><rect x=\"844\" y=\"255\" width=\"232\" height=\"7\" rx=\"2\"/></g>\n    <rect x=\"870\" y=\"120\" width=\"180\" height=\"38\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#222B36\" stroke=\"#C9D1DA\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n    <!-- red tag pin on damage -->\n    <circle cx=\"1079\" cy=\"300\" r=\"17\" fill=\"#FF6C6C\"/><text x=\"1079\" y=\"306\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"IBM Plex Sans,sans-serif\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#0B1016\">!</text>\n    <!-- card -->\n    <g><rect x=\"1096\" y=\"250\" width=\"150\" height=\"60\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#0B1016\" stroke=\"#222B36\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"1110\" y=\"274\" font-family=\"IBM Plex Mono,monospace\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#FF6C6C\">RED · LOCATED</text><text x=\"1110\" y=\"294\" font-family=\"IBM Plex Sans,sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#8B95A1\">alert sent to repair</text></g>\n    <text x=\"960\" y=\"398\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"IBM Plex Sans,sans-serif\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#D95A00\">Caught, mapped &amp; actioned</text>\n  </svg>";
export const html = "<p class=\"lead\">“We inspect our racks regularly.” It’s a reassuring phrase — and a dangerous one when it isn’t backed by process, structure and evidence.</p>\n    <p>In most warehouses, rack inspections are still conducted manually, based on visual memory, recorded in notebooks or spreadsheets, carried out by non-specialists, and done infrequently or only after something goes wrong. On the surface it looks like safety is handled. The real question isn’t <em>whether</em> inspections happen — it’s <strong>how</strong>.</p>\n    <p>Manual inspections often fail to document what was seen in a way anyone can trace. They’re open to interpretation bias, missed issues, and — under pressure — reporting that gets filled in after the fact. A bent upright or fresh impact damage can go nowhere if it isn’t escalated properly. With warehouses running at tighter tolerances and higher densities, that’s a gap you can’t leave to memory. This is where digital inspection stops being a nice-to-have: it doesn’t just capture problems, it drives the action, and it’s a reliable way to keep things consistent across shifts, sites and teams.</p>\n\n    <h2 id=\"phases\">Every inspection has four phases</h2>\n    <ul class=\"clean\">\n      <li><strong>Pre-inspection</strong> — identify high-risk zones, arrange access, verify the layout.</li>\n      <li><strong>Inspection</strong> — capture the visual evidence and record what’s found.</li>\n      <li><strong>Post-inspection</strong> — classify, escalate the red zones, produce an actionable report.</li>\n      <li><strong>Repair &amp; replacement</strong> — make sure recommendations are acted on, closed and verified.</li>\n    </ul>\n    <p>Manual processes tend to break down across all four — most badly at the hand-offs between them.</p>\n\n    <h2 id=\"manual\">Manual inspections: where they fall short</h2>\n    <ul class=\"clean gap\">\n      <li><strong>Subjective observations</strong> — two inspectors can classify the same damage differently.</li>\n      <li><strong>Inconsistent classification</strong> — EN 15635’s Green/Amber/Red thresholds get interpreted differently, so damage is under-reported or misjudged.</li>\n      <li><strong>Inconsistent action</strong> — even once tagged, what actually gets done about a Red or Amber varies from inspector to inspector.</li>\n      <li><strong>No visual traceability</strong> — issues are described, not shown.</li>\n      <li><strong>Paper gets lost</strong> — no audit trail, no history to refer back to.</li>\n      <li><strong>Delayed action</strong> — reports have to be typed, signed and escalated by hand.</li>\n      <li><strong>No analytics</strong> — you can’t see trends, hotspots or repeat offenders.</li>\n      <li><strong>Back-filling risk</strong> — missed inspections are sometimes filled in afterwards, which quietly undermines the whole exercise — a real concern across multi-site operations where physical verification is weak.</li>\n      <li><strong>Laborious BoQ</strong> — building a bill of quantities for repairs from scattered notes, photos and sketches is slow and error-prone.</li>\n      <li><strong>Hard to pinpoint on drawings</strong> — without a digital map or Digital Twin, locating damage accurately on the site plan is painful, and leads to miscommunication and wrong repairs.</li>\n    </ul>\n    <p>Manual inspections often feel productive. In reality they leave critical blind spots.</p>\n\n    <h2 id=\"digital\">Digital inspections: what they add</h2>\n    <ul class=\"clean\">\n      <li><strong>Photo-tagged observations</strong> — every issue captured visually and mapped to its exact location.</li>\n      <li><strong>Consistent classification</strong> — Green/Amber/Red applied against the same criteria each time, reducing inspector-to-inspector variation.</li>\n      <li><strong>Reports without the delay</strong> — generated and shareable straight away, not typed up later.</li>\n      <li><strong>Traceability</strong> — a history of how, when and where issues occurred, for real root-cause analysis.</li>\n      <li><strong>Analytics &amp; trends</strong> — recurring problem zones, repeat damage types, and comparisons across facilities.</li>\n      <li><strong>Integrated escalation</strong> — a Red finding pushes an alert to the responsible team, cutting downtime.</li>\n      <li><strong>BoQ automation</strong> — the bill of quantities builds itself from the tagged locations and damage types.</li>\n      <li><strong>Drawing-integrated maps</strong> — issues overlaid on the warehouse plan or a 3D Digital Twin, easy to locate and act on.</li>\n      <li><strong>Closure tracking</strong> — each issue followed through repair or replacement to full closure, with an accountability log.</li>\n    </ul>\n    <p class=\"pquote\">Digital inspections don’t just record problems — they create accountability and measurable insight.</p>\n\n    <h2 id=\"compare\">Manual vs digital, side by side</h2>\n    <table class=\"tbl\">\n      <tr><th>&nbsp;</th><th>Manual</th><th>Digital</th></tr>\n      <tr><td>Observations</td><td class=\"m\">Described from memory</td><td class=\"r\">Photo-tagged and located</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Classification</td><td class=\"m\">Interpreted differently</td><td class=\"r\">Applied consistently (G/A/R)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Traceability</td><td class=\"m\">Notebook/Excel — can be lost</td><td class=\"r\">Retained history &amp; audit trail</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Action</td><td class=\"m\">Typed, signed, delayed</td><td class=\"r\">Escalated immediately</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Analytics</td><td class=\"m\">None</td><td class=\"r\">Trends, hotspots, repeat zones</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Bill of quantities</td><td class=\"m\">Manual, error-prone</td><td class=\"r\">Auto-generated from tags</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Locating on drawings</td><td class=\"m\">Hand-sketched</td><td class=\"r\">Mapped on the plan / Digital Twin</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Closure</td><td class=\"m\">Hard to track</td><td class=\"r\">Tracked to closure</td></tr>\n    </table>\n\n    <h2 id=\"standard\">What EN 15635 says</h2>\n    <ul class=\"clean\">\n      <li>Appoint a <strong>Person Responsible for Storage Equipment Safety (PRSES)</strong> to ensure inspections happen.</li>\n      <li>Carry out regular visual checks by staff, and an <strong>expert inspection at least annually</strong>, at intervals set by risk assessment.</li>\n      <li>Classify damage systematically and respond appropriately.</li>\n      <li>Keep documentation <strong>traceable and retained</strong> — exactly what a digital system does far better than paper.</li>\n    </ul>\n\n    <h2 id=\"myths\">Common misconceptions</h2>\n    <table class=\"tbl\">\n      <tr><th>The myth</th><th>The reality</th></tr>\n      <tr><td class=\"m\">We already do inspections</td><td class=\"r\">If it isn’t visualised, digitised and trended, it isn’t complete.</td></tr>\n      <tr><td class=\"m\">Our staff know what to look for</td><td class=\"r\">Trained? Calibrated? Working to EN 15635 criteria?</td></tr>\n      <tr><td class=\"m\">Paper reports are good enough</td><td class=\"r\">They give no traceability, no escalation, no data-driven insight.</td></tr>\n    </table>\n\n    <h2 id=\"outcomes\">Same damage, two outcomes</h2>\n    <div class=\"illus\"><span class=\"lbl\">Illustrative scenario</span>\n      <figure style=\"margin:14px 0 4px\">\n        <svg class=\"art\" viewBox=\"0 0 900 380\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A bent upright is found. On the manual path it has no photo or tag, the report sits, and the upright fails. On the digital path it is photo-tagged and located, the repair team is notified, and it is braced and replaced.\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\">\n          <rect width=\"900\" height=\"380\" fill=\"#0B1016\"/>\n          <rect x=\"330\" y=\"18\" width=\"240\" height=\"46\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#C9D1DA\"/><text x=\"450\" y=\"46\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"IBM Plex Sans,sans-serif\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#0B1016\">A bent upright is found</text>\n          <path d=\"M400 64 L230 96\" stroke=\"#4D5A69\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" marker-end=\"url(#a1)\"/>\n          <path d=\"M500 64 L670 96\" stroke=\"#54DE91\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" marker-end=\"url(#a2)\"/>\n          <text x=\"230\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"IBM Plex Mono,monospace\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"600\" letter-spacing=\"1\" fill=\"#8B95A1\">MANUAL</text>\n          <text x=\"670\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"IBM Plex Mono,monospace\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"600\" letter-spacing=\"1\" fill=\"#2BCB74\">DIGITAL</text>\n          <!-- manual column -->\n          <g font-family=\"IBM Plex Sans,sans-serif\">\n            <rect x=\"110\" y=\"104\" width=\"240\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#141B24\" stroke=\"#2F3A47\"/><text x=\"230\" y=\"131\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#8B95A1\">No photo, no tag</text>\n            <rect x=\"110\" y=\"176\" width=\"240\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#141B24\" stroke=\"#2F3A47\"/><text x=\"230\" y=\"203\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#8B95A1\">Report sits, not escalated</text>\n            <rect x=\"110\" y=\"248\" width=\"240\" height=\"52\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2A1416\" stroke=\"#FF6C6C\"/><text x=\"230\" y=\"271\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#FF6C6C\">Fails after further impact</text><text x=\"230\" y=\"290\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#FF6C6C\">✕ avoidable failure</text>\n          </g>\n          <!-- digital column -->\n          <g font-family=\"IBM Plex Sans,sans-serif\">\n            <rect x=\"550\" y=\"104\" width=\"240\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#11261B\" stroke=\"#1F5A3B\"/><text x=\"670\" y=\"131\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2BCB74\">Photo + Red tag, located</text>\n            <rect x=\"550\" y=\"176\" width=\"240\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#11261B\" stroke=\"#1F5A3B\"/><text x=\"670\" y=\"203\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2BCB74\">Repair team auto-notified</text>\n            <rect x=\"550\" y=\"248\" width=\"240\" height=\"52\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#54DE91\"/><text x=\"670\" y=\"271\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#0B1016\">Braced &amp; replaced</text><text x=\"670\" y=\"290\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#11261B\">✓ resolved in days</text>\n          </g>\n          <g stroke=\"#4D5A69\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"230\" y1=\"148\" x2=\"230\" y2=\"174\" marker-end=\"url(#a1)\"/><line x1=\"230\" y1=\"220\" x2=\"230\" y2=\"246\" marker-end=\"url(#a1)\"/></g>\n          <g stroke=\"#54DE91\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"670\" y1=\"148\" x2=\"670\" y2=\"174\" marker-end=\"url(#a2)\"/><line x1=\"670\" y1=\"220\" x2=\"670\" y2=\"246\" marker-end=\"url(#a2)\"/></g>\n          <defs>\n            <marker id=\"a1\" markerWidth=\"9\" markerHeight=\"9\" refX=\"4\" refY=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><polygon points=\"0,0 8,0 4,8\" fill=\"#4D5A69\"/></marker>\n            <marker id=\"a2\" markerWidth=\"9\" markerHeight=\"9\" refX=\"4\" refY=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><polygon points=\"0,0 8,0 4,8\" fill=\"#54DE91\"/></marker>\n          </defs>\n        </svg>\n      </figure>\n      <p style=\"font-size:15px;color:var(--muted);margin:6px 0 14px\">Same warehouse, same issue — a different method, an entirely different outcome.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <p>Manual inspections are a good start. But they can’t match the speed, visibility and traceability of digital ones. If your racks are critical infrastructure, your inspection method should be too — driven by real data, not gut feel.</p>\n\n    <div class=\"cta\">\n      <h3>See the digital difference</h3>\n      <p>Book a demo to see how RAMS turns inspections into action — tagged, mapped, escalated and closed.</p>\n      <a class=\"btn\" href=\"/company/contact\">Book a demo</a>\n    </div>";
